  write("README.md",`# Dash Punch - Core Edition\n\nUnzip the whole folder. Open index.html for offline play.\n\nFor controllers and online play, use Node.js 20 or newer: run npm start in this\nfolder and open http://localhost:8080. The server has no third-party dependencies.\nOnline friends need a reachable hosted server/HTTPS address; sending this ZIP\ndoes not create an internet room server. Both peers must use this Core Edition.\n\n## Included\n\n${characters.length} fighters: ${characters.map(key=>coreCharacters[key].name).join(", ")}.\n\n${coreStages.length} fighting stages: ${coreStages.map(stage=>stage.name).join(", ")}. Dashball and Sandbag stages are also included.\n\nTwo-button combat, 1-10 local player/controller slots, CPU opponents, teams,\ncontroller remapping, graphics quality, directional shields, techs, Chase,\nKickoffs and all existing core-character mechanics are preserved.\nPrivate online play is 1v1 with rollback, on Crosswire.\n\nLocal and Online menu art uses the actual core fighter sprites.\n\nExperimental fighters/stages and their sprite packs are absent. Developer\nStage Builder, Quick Playtest and Showcase entry points are omitted. The full\ndevelopment project is unchanged and remains the place to create custom stages.\nNo screenshot galleries, old builds, test fixtures or development dependencies\nare included. See CREDITS.txt and build-manifest.json.\n`);
